==Serbo-Croatian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|sh|čȍvek||Ekavian}}
* {{alter|sh|čovik|človik||Ikavian|Čakavian}}
* {{alter|sh|človek||archaic|Kajkavian}}
* {{alter|sh|človjek||obsolete}}
* {{alter|sh|čoek|čojek|čȏk||regional|colloquial}}

===Etymology===
From older {{m|sh|človjek}}, from {{der|sh|sla-pro|*čьlověkъ}}, {{m|sla-pro|*čelověkъ}}, from {{inh|sh|ine-bsl-pro|*kelawaikas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sh-IPA|čòvjek}} or {{sh-IPA|čȍvjek}}
* {{hyphenation|sh|čo|vjek}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=čòvjek|head2=čȍvjek}}

# [[man]], [[person]]
#: {{ux|sh|Jeste li vid(j)eli ovog čov(j)eka?|t=Have you seen this man?|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|sh|Ti si mrtav čov(j)ek.|t=You're a dead man.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|sh|Zanemarite čov(j)eka iza zav(j)ese.|t=Pay no attention to the man behind the curtain.|inline=1}}
# [[human]]
#: {{ux|sh|Ne želim biti čov(j)ek, želim biti robot!|t=I don't want to be human, I want to be a robot!|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|sh|Nisi zao, samo si...čov(j)ek.|t=You're not evil, you're just...human.|inline=1}}
# [[person]] of [[integrity]], [[mensch]]
#* {{quote-book|1=sh|author=Vuk Stefanović Karadžić|authorlink=Vuk Stefanović Karadžić|title=Srpske narodne poslovice [Serbian Folk Proverbs]|url=https://archive.org/details/srpskenarodnepos00kara/page/26|location=Beč|year=1849|page=27|text=Боље се с '''чоеком''' побити него с рђом целивати. <small>У Грбљу.</small>|tr=Bolje se s '''čoekom''' pobiti nego s rđom celivati. <small>U Grblju.</small>|t=It is better to fight with a [proper] man than to kiss with an unworthy one [literally: to kiss with rust]. <small>From [[w:Grbalj|Grbalj]].</small>}}
# used as an indefinite, general subject; any person in a given situation
#* {{quote-book|1=sh|author=Ante Kovačić|authorlink=Ante Kovačić|title=Fiškal [The Advocate]|url=https://lektire.skole.hr/djela/fiskal/|location=Zagreb|year=1882|year_published=2013|publisher=Bulaja naklada|isbn=978-953-328-202-2|page=28|text=Vrijeme i narav bijahu neopisivo sumorni. U takvim časovima '''čovjek''' biva zlovoljan, dremovan i nezadovoljan.|t=The weather and nature were indescribably dismal. In such moments, one becomes ill-willed, drowsy and dissatisfied.}}


